The MUI2 UI foundation is adapted from GTNewHorizons/GT5-Unofficial:
https://github.com/GTNewHorizons/GT5-Unofficial/tree/f0472cfbd44ab9c8d5a27df7e98c64a42eb1c03f

Upstream source revision: f0472cfbd44ab9c8d5a27df7e98c64a42eb1c03f.
License: GNU LGPL v3; see the accompanying GTNH-LGPL-3.0 file.

The theme builder, theme keys, texture IDs, core texture declarations, steam
texture variants, progressbar theme and modular screen are adapted for this
project's Java 8 API. GTNH addon-specific integrations are excluded.

The native Cover, CoverContext, CoverFactory, CoverPlacer, CoverRegistry,
CoverRegistration, CoverPlacementPredicate, CoverLegacyData and CoverNone APIs
are adapted from the same revision. CoverableTileEntity ports object ownership,
attachment lifecycle, per-side persistence and synchronization into this fork's
existing machine and pipe base classes. The old integer APIs are deprecated
compatibility views; attached Cover objects own the persistent state.
CoverLegacyBehavior and NativeCoverBehavior preserve existing addon behaviors
while native cover implementations use the object API and MUI2 directly.

PNG resources under textures/gui/mui2 are copied from that revision without
image changes. Their source paths and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in
GTNH-MUI2-ASSETS.json. They are isolated from the existing GUI resources.
Some texture declarations in upstream point to missing optional primitive
variants; those use the corresponding standard texture as an explicit fallback.
The neutral ingot and disabled power icon are copied from the same revision's
miscutils and tectech resource namespaces. The manifest records every fallback.

Upstream credits include Jimbno / UU-Tex and GTNH texture contributors.

GTFluidSlot reuses this fork's existing GT_FluidDisplayStackRenderer for its
amount label, retaining the original precision, font scale and positioning.
